[0.148, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[6G\u001b[2m     \u001b[22m le`, `client_model` refuse it, `client_serve` plays as before, sanitised too. No hash pin moved. |\u001b[K\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m274 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m|\u001b[14G— / L41c | Stage 5's loose ends, the third part: stripped release binaries, their debug files kept. \r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m  \u001b[10G +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m**Done\u001b[19G2026-11-28**: a served test's crash reports under its own state directory, never the real home'\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242ms; every distributed program links with a SHA-1 build ID (`manifest_distributed`); `scripts/stage-bund\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mle.sh` keeps each one's debug file as `debug-<bundle>/.build-id/<xx>/<rest>.debug`, packed beside the \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mbundle as `debug-<bundle>.tar.gz`, and strips it (`objcopy --strip-all`); `manifest --serve` installs \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mJettison's crash handler, reports in `$XDG_STATE_HOME/manifest/crashes`. Met: the staged programs have\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m no `.debug_*` or `.symtab` and keep their build IDs, equal to the debug files'; `test-bundle.sh host`\r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m passes on the stripped bundle; bundle_smoke, packaging, bundle_fresh_home, cli_*, token_*, validate_*\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m, distribution pass in clang-debug (31) and clang-release (32); a SIGSEGV of the stripped server under\r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m `env -i` with no addr2line wrote a report that symbolise-crash.sh named against the debug tarball as \u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mthe unstripped binary names it; restaging gave the same bytes for both tarballs. |                    \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[2m 275 \r\u001b[1B\u001b[22m \u001b[3G   \u001b[2m 276 \u001b[22m W01 is technically ind\u001b[35Gpendent of N01–N03; its later\u001b[65Gplacement\u001b[75Gis\u001b[78Gthe\u001b[82Gdefault\u001b[90Gpriority,\r\u001b[1B     \u001b[2m 277 \u001b[22m not a dependency on transport. Likewise, W05, W07 and W08 can be\u001b[77Gdeveloped\u001b[87Gseparately\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;223;134;102mHonking…\u001b[13G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m6m 12s\u001b[20G· ↓\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m7.3k\u001b[29Gtokens)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[20C\u001b[6B\u001b[38;2;0;204;204m4\u001b[39m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[20;3H\u001b[?25h"]
