[0.025, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[6G\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 6 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m| — / L54 | A new player names their starting ship as they found their company (D-123). **Done 2026-11-2\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m   -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m8**: `Company::Provision` carries the ship's name; the ship saves it (`World::Ship::displayName`) and `Q\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m   -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242muery::ShipView` carries it, over the network too. The handler trims both names of spaces and refuses eac\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m   -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mh `NameEmpty`, `NameTooLong` (over `kMaxNameCodePoints`, 32 code points) or `NameNotPrintable` (not UTF-\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m   -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m8, or a control character); the company's name had no checks before. A ship no player names takes `Defau\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m   -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mltShipName`'s, its company's name and numeral: NPC traders' (`Nia Freight 1`), a claimed grant's, and th\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m   -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242me console's `provision` with no ship name. The client's start screen gains the ship's field, `found <com\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m   -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mpany name> <ship name>`, and the company, flight and service screens show a ship by its name, in four la\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m   -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mnguages. Exit criterion met: `client_serve` founds \"Ada Freight\" and \"Long Shot\" with `found` and reads \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m   -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mthe ship's name on the company screen before and after the server's restart; `client_screens` through th\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m   -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242me start screen; `company` refuses an empty, too long and unprintable name of either, naming why. Five wo\r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m   -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mrld hash pins moved, bytes alone. |                                                                     \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 2 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mFree: parked on feature-base. L54 merged 2026-11-28, awaiting the batch gate.                           \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mRunning \u001b[1m7\u001b[22m shell commands…\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  $ git -C '/home/ivan/projects/jettison' status --porcelain\r\u001b[17C\u001b[2B5m 12s · ↓\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m8.7k tokens)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[18C\u001b[6B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m(shift+tab to cycle)\u001b[39m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[21;3H\u001b[?25h"]
