[0.054, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[3G-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mTheme:\u001b[22m the game UI now changes with \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mdev.palette\u001b[39m, and Latte draws a light panel with dark text.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mItalic:\u001b[22m \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mem\u001b[39m draws in Roboto Italic. The font is the OFL-licensed copy that ships with Tracy, with its licence beside\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bit, and it's the regular weight because no Medium Italic exists.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mChecks:\u001b[22m the ui and app tests pass, all 13 reference views are unchanged, and the smoke test passes. It hasn't\u001b[115Gbeen\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bthrough the batch gate yet.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BOne part of the brief was wrong. A missing font face wasn't silent: RmlUi already logs each text drawn without a\u001b[116Gface,\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Band the UI counts that as a problem. So no new warning was added. The agent asked whether you still want exactly\u001b[116Gone\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bwarning per missing face. I'd leave it as RmlUi does it, since the existing message names the face and the element.\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BThe player setting for the palette is still open on J26, for a game's own settings screen.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BJettison lane B is free again. I'm leaving it idle unless you want J29, the rover's grip. L37, L41 and J12 are still\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Brunning.\u001b[K\r\u001b[109C\u001b[12B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m3\u001b[39m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[19;3H\u001b[?25h"]
[0.030, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[15B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m✻\u001b[3GWaiting for \u001b[1m3\u001b[22m background\u001b[28Gagent\u001b[35Gto finish\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[3B❯ \u001b[2mhow are the lanes getting on?\r\u001b[67C\u001b[3B\u001b[22m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m← 1\u001b[72Gagent · ↓ to\u001b[85Gmanage\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[19;3H\u001b[?25h"]
