[0.124, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[6G\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m    -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mhe binary archive as a `Physics.Shape` of version 1, the same shape the same bytes, under the new world\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m    -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m directory `collision/` (`Host::kWorldDirectories`), so a server's pack and the world's digest hold it \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m    -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mand no model; `ReadCollisionFile` reads one through the VFS, and `ConvexHullPoints` simplifies points w\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m    -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mith Jolt's convex hull builder. `jettison_bake_collision` (`source/tools/collision`) bakes one through \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m    -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m`Bake::CollisionShape`, the library the cook is to call: `collision-<name>` nodes are convex hulls, `co\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m    -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mllision-mesh-<name>` meshes, and a model with neither a convex hull of each mesh node of at most 32 poi\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m    -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mnts. A dock vehicle names one (`VehicleDefinition::collision`, optional, so every file reads as before)\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m    -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m and collides as it, a mesh refused. The physics suite drops crates on a file's pods and the keel betwe\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m    -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242men them where the box would hold them; the baker's suite bakes a model with `collision-` nodes and one \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m    -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mwithout, the same bytes twice; `bake_collision_cli` runs the tool; the dock suite defines a vehicle fro\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m    -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mm one. No pin moved ([physics](physics.md#a-models-collision-shape), [decisions](decisions.md#physics))\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m   