[0.096, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[6G\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mWhat it does:\u001b[22m after a lost connection the client dials again, at most once a second, with the same token. The\u001b[115Gstatus\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bline says it's reconnecting, in all four languages. Once back, it resends the requests it never heard complete,\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bunder their original sequence numbers.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mTests:\u001b[22m they cover the same four cases as the terminal UI's: a lost buy runs exactly once, a request made while\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Breconnecting is sent, a refused one isn't resent, and a revoked token stops the redialling.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mShared code:\u001b[22m the rule for which closed connections get redialled now lives in the shared \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mremote\u001b[39m module, used by\u001b[117Gboth\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bthe client and the terminal UI.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mDecision:\u001b[22m recorded as D-126.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mFixed at merge:\u001b[22m one tidy finding, a list filled in a loop without reserving its size first.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B \u001b[3GThe new\u001b[11Gte\u001b[14Gt was \u001b[21Gnly run\u001b[29Gagainst\u001b[37Gthe\u001b[41Gin-process\u001b[52Gserver;\u001b[60Gthe\u001b[64Gagent\u001b[70Gdidn't\u001b[77Gtry\u001b[81Ga\u001b[83Glive\u001b[88Gclient\u001b[95Gagainst\u001b[103Ga\u001b[105Gkilled\u001b[112Gserver.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B  Manifest lane C is free again. L37 and the two Jettison rendering\u001b[69Glanes\u001b[75Gare\u001b[79Gstill\u001b[85Grunning.\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m·\u001b[19G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m7\u001b[26G2\u001b[28G2\u001b[39m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[19;3H\u001b[?25h"]
