[0.083, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[6G\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m    -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242md its own velocity and arrives with its target frame's, relative to its carrier, on Jettison's end spee\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m    -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mds where the profile meets them and a drift for the rest (a crossing drive drifts it all; the power law\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m    -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m still eases), retiring W22b's motion blend, its re-plotting and `Cruising::departureBody`/`arrivalBody\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m    -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m` (now `departureVelocity`/`arrivalVelocity`); bodies in the way placed where the ship passes nearest t\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m    -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mhem as flown (`kPassSamples`, 64, closer at the ends); turns bent round on 16-point curves; a cruise to\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m    -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m a ship (`Cruise::targetShip`, 1 km off, re-aimed each step, broken off if lost); `Space::BreakOffCruis\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m    -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242me` (`CruiseBrokenOff`, `NotCruising`); a ship that came out at rest (`Space::CameOut`) moved 250 m off \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m    -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mby the next arrival in its place (D-125). Each tested in `space` (98 cases). Pins moved: company by byt\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m    -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mes (the new component, proven by reverting its registration), fixture_alone by CameOut, fixture, fixtur\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m    -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242me_governance and fixture_development by CameOut and the bodies' placement (proven by reverting both); f\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m    -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mlight's held. All 69 Debug suites pass. With the pin move to Jettison 01eeae8 (requires by identifier, \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m   